    "Alex Morgan has 8 years of Python experience (since 2018).",
    "Employers: Contoso Logistics, Senior Backend Engineer (Mar 2022 - present); Fabrikam Health, Backend Engineer (Feb 2020 - Feb 2022); Tailspin Analytics, Python Developer (Jan 2018 - Jan 2020). Alex never worked at Northwind Pay or at any payments company.",
    "Shipment events pipeline (Contoso Logistics): SQS standard queue + Lambda consumers, idempotent by carrier event ID with a unique constraint; 2 million events per day; webhook timeouts 4% -> 0.1%; endpoint p95 2.5 s -> 80 ms; zero duplicate status updates since launch.",
    "Tracking API latency (Contoso Logistics): p95 900 ms -> 120 ms; N+1 from 12 queries to 2 per request; Redis cache-aside with a 30-second TTL invalidated on status-change events; DB CPU 70% -> 35%; Black Friday at 3x traffic with the same 4 containers; the tech lead's Go rewrite was dropped after a one-week profiling spike.",
    "Appointment report query (Fabrikam Health): table with 40 million rows; 14 s -> 180 ms; composite index on (clinic_id, scheduled_at) created concurrently; counting moved to ORM annotate/aggregate.",
    "Duplicate reminder incident (Fabrikam Health): Alex enabled Celery acks_late; a long batch task exceeded the Redis visibility timeout and was redelivered; 3,000 patients got a duplicate SMS; found 2 hours later from support tickets; after the fix (one task per reminder, unique sent record, structured logs, Sentry, retry alert) a later spike was detected in 5 minutes.",
    "CI pipeline speed-up (Contoso Logistics): 35 min -> 8 min; flaky failures 15/week -> 1; coverage 58% -> 85%; weekly -> daily deploys; pytest-xdist, Postgres service container per job in GitHub Actions, rolling deploy to ECS.",
    "Nightly sales ETL (Tailspin Analytics): pandas + Airflow, one task per region; 6 hours -> 50 minutes; peak memory 14 GB -> 3 GB.",
    "Kubernetes: basic usage only (deploys with Helm charts maintained by another team, kubectl logs/describe); never designed or operated a cluster. No Kafka, Rust, Go or Java in production. No ML model training.",
    "Certification: AWS Certified Developer - Associate (2023).",
    "Technical: SQS standard queues are at-least-once with best-effort ordering; default visibility timeout is 30 seconds; Lambda maximum timeout is 15 minutes; CPython's GIL lets one thread run bytecode at a time and is released during blocking I/O; Python 3.13 added an optional experimental free-threaded build.",
    "Salary: Alex never gives a number; he asks for the budgeted range."
